# dsh-crossnet-link - git line-ending policy
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: git's own core.autocrlf (true on many Windows machines) rewrites
# LF to CRLF in the working tree at checkout time. This repository is text-only and every
# file in it is LF, with exactly two documented exceptions (the captured console-output
# fixtures, which record what a Windows tool actually printed - see .editorconfig). Without
# this file a fresh clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true would produce CRLF files,
# and the release gate (repo-hygiene.ps1) would report non-zero line-ending notes.
#
# LAST UPDATED  : 2026-09-24 (README closeout: added together with the first git commit)
# COMMANDS USED : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File | % { ... }"
#                 (line-ending census, see repo-hygiene.ps1 section 6)
#
# Rule 1: every file is text and stays LF in the working tree, whatever the local
#         core.autocrlf setting is.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rule 2: the two captured-output fixtures are byte evidence, not source - git must not
#         touch their CRLF endings at all.
tests/fixtures/*.json -text

# Rule 3: binaries (should not exist here; the repository is text-only by policy)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
